      "hints": [
        "With the material and length unchanged, resistance is inversely proportional to cross-sectional area.",
        "A circular area is proportional to r², so first determine the area factor when the radius is doubled."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For the same material and length, R = ρL / A, so resistance is inversely proportional to cross-sectional area.",
        "The area of the circular rod is proportional to r².",
        "Doubling r makes the area four times larger, so the resistance becomes one quarter of its original value.",
        "Therefore the resistance decreases by a factor of four."
      ],
