      "hints": [
        "Young modulus is tensile stress divided by tensile strain, and strain is extension divided by original length.",
        "Rearrange the combined relationship to extension = stress × original length / Young modulus."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Young modulus is E = stress / strain, with strain = extension / original length.",
        "Rearrange to extension = stress × original length / E.",
        "extension = (1.9 × 10⁶ × 0.12) / (1.3 × 10¹¹) m = 1.75 × 10⁻⁶ m.",
        "Therefore the extension is 1.8 × 10⁻⁶ m."
